# Tools Hub

Left sidebar entry (Wrench icon, `SidebarTabKey.Tools`, always visible). All utility features live under `/tools/*` with a shared left sub-navigation panel.

## Current tools

| Tool | Route | DB table |
|------|-------|----------|
| Picbed (image hosting) | `/tools/picbed` | `picbed_images` |
| Password Generator | `/tools/password` | none |
| API Tester | `/tools/apitest` | none |

## Key files

- Sidebar nav entry: `src/app/[variants]/(main)/_layout/Desktop/SideBar/TopActions.tsx`
- Tools sub-nav: `src/app/[variants]/(main)/tools/_layout/Desktop/Nav.tsx`
- Shared layout: `src/app/[variants]/(main)/tools/_layout/Desktop/`
- i18n namespace: `src/locales/default/tools.ts` + `locales/en-US/tools.json` + `locales/zh-CN/tools.json`

## Adding a new tool

1. Create `src/app/[variants]/(main)/tools/[tool-name]/page.tsx`.
2. Add i18n keys to `src/locales/default/tools.ts` + both `en-US` and `zh-CN` JSONs.
3. Add DB migration SQL + register in `packages/database/migrations/meta/_journal.json`.
4. Add tRPC router in `src/server/routers/lambda/` + register in `lambda/index.ts`.
5. Add nav entry in `Nav.tsx`.
6. Add route to middleware matcher in `src/middleware.ts`.

## API Tester safety notes

API Tester sends user-entered URLs through the server-side proxy at
`src/app/(backend)/webapi/tools/apitest/route.ts`, which delegates to
`src/server/services/apiTester/index.ts`.

- Keep outbound requests behind `ssrfSafeFetch`; do not replace it with raw
  `fetch` on the server.
- Thread cancellation and timeout signals to the actual outbound fetch. Client
  cancellation alone only aborts the browser-to-ChatHub request.
- Do not persist request secrets in browser storage. History entries must
  redact bearer tokens, basic passwords, API keys, Authorization/Cookie-style
  headers, and query API key values before entering localStorage.
- cURL import/export is best-effort but should match documented cURL behavior
  for supported flags. In particular, `-G` / `--get` moves `-d` data into the
  query string, `--json` implies a JSON request body plus JSON headers, and
  short options may attach their values (`-XPOST`, `-dfoo=bar`). Reject
  unsupported methods or ambiguous option combinations instead of importing a
  misleading request.
- Request body support must stay aligned across `BODY_METHODS`, the request UI,
  payload builder, cURL export, and server service. GET and HEAD do not send
  bodies; POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, and OPTIONS may.
- Normalize stored history requests through current draft defaults before
  rendering or restoring them. Repair valid legacy header rows and discard
  entries with unsupported methods or unusable request shapes.
- Global request shortcuts must not fire while an API Tester modal or drawer is
  open. History restore/delete actions must be keyboard accessible.
- Response tabs are labeled `Response Body` and `Response Headers`. Every new
  response resets the outer panel to `Response Body`.
- Valid JSON responses expose `Tree | Formatted | Raw` and default to `Tree`;
  non-JSON, malformed, empty, or oversized JSON responses expose only the safe
  text views and default to `Formatted`. A new response must reset this local
  mode based on the new body.
- Build JSON trees with a fixed node budget (`JSON_TREE_MAX_NODES`) and return
  an explicit overflow result instead of partial tree data. Oversized valid JSON
  stays available through Formatted/Raw with a localized explanation.
- Use Ant Design `Tree` with a fixed virtualized height and an accessible name;
  preserve its native focus, expansion, and keyboard behavior. Render stable
  one-line rows so virtualization measurements remain reliable.
- Copy uses pretty JSON in Tree/Formatted and exact response text in Raw.
  Download always uses the exact original response body.
- All visible strings belong in `src/locales/default/tools.ts` and both served
  locale JSON files.
